/marketing:campaign-plan Promote the New Arrivals collection ahead of two gifting occasions, to our email list.

Products: Horizon Handbag ($260), Noir Clutch ($185), Orbit Handbag ($170), Drift Wallet ($85), Ember Wallet ($85), Ascent Card Case ($85), Roam Keyring ($85), Naxos ($80), Capri ($65) — all from usa.jafferjees.com/collections/new-arrivals.

Audience segments, based on the site’s own nav (Men / Women / Travel / Work / Gift Set — Work is explicitly “for Men & Women,” not men-only; exclude Corporate, that’s a separate B2B inquiry channel, not a retail audience):

Men’s segment → wallets, card case, keyring
Women’s segment → handbags, clutch
Gifting segment (either gender) → all items, framed around complimentary gift wrap and engraving
Timing — run as two separate waves, not one campaign, since they’re on different calendars and have different lead times:

Eid-ul-Fitr wave (expected ~March 9–10, 2027, moon-sighting dependent): 4 weeks of email, starting the first Monday of February 2027.
Christmas wave (Dec 25): must send much earlier to clear the ~2–3 day processing + up to 15 working days delivery window, plus allow for the 3-working-day exchange deadline if something needs fixing before Christmas. Start this wave in early-to-mid November, not December.
Copy rules: never guarantee a delivery date — use “order by [date] to receive in time” phrasing tied to the “up to X working days” shipping language, not a promise. Don’t assume or state customers’ religion; segment by occasion/timing, not by inferred religious identity.

Budget: small. Email only, no paid ads. No discount or sale — new arrivals only.

Source of truth: the live site (usa.jafferjees.com) always overrides brand/voice.md, prior findings, or anything stated earlier in this plan. If anything in this brief mismatches the live site when you check it, flag the specific mismatch to me before proceeding — don’t silently correct it.

